.TH SWEETSIDLE 1 "September 2026" "sweetsidle 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sweetsidle \- Wayland idle management daemon for the Sweets compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sweetsidle
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B sweetsidle status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B sweetsidle pause
.br
.B sweetsidle resume
.br
.B sweetsidle reload
.br
.B sweetsidle
.RB [ \-c | \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.B \-\-check-config
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sweetsidle
is a lightweight Wayland idle management daemon and the recommended idle
daemon for the Sweets compositor.
It uses the
.B ext-idle-notify-v1
protocol to run configured commands after periods of inactivity and when input
resumes.
.PP
The daemon can also run commands before sleep, after resume, and in response to
logind lock and unlock requests.
It respects compositor, ScreenSaver D-Bus, and systemd-logind idle inhibitors
by default.
.PP
With no command,
.B sweetsidle
loads its configuration and remains in the foreground until it receives a
termination signal or encounters a fatal runtime error.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the daemon's running or paused state, idle-hint state, listener state, and
tracked D-Bus and systemd inhibitors.
The daemon must already be running.
.TP
.B "status --json"
Emit the same live snapshot as one compact JSON object followed by a newline.
The object contains
.BR schema_version ,
.BR paused ,
.BR idle_hint ,
.BR listeners ,
and
.BR inhibitors .
This form is intended for scripts and status bars.
.TP
.B pause
Suspend every idle listener and clear the logind idle hint.
Commands already running and explicit sleep, resume, lock, and unlock hooks are
not interrupted.
Repeating the command is harmless.
.TP
.B resume
Resume idle detection and start every listener with a fresh timeout.
Actions that became due while paused do not run immediately.
Repeating the command is harmless.
.TP
.B reload
Queue a reload of the active configuration through the control socket.
The response confirms the request was queued; check daemon logs for validation
and application results.
If a reload is already pending, the response reports that it is pending.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-c " PATH ", \-\-config " PATH
Read configuration from
.I PATH
instead of the default path.
.TP
.B \-\-check-config
Parse and validate the selected configuration, report the result, and exit
without connecting to Wayland or starting the daemon.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable debug-level runtime logging.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print machine-readable output for the
.B status
command.
It is rejected with other commands and during daemon startup.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The default configuration path is
.IR ~/.config/sweetsidle/config.toml .
The file uses TOML and rejects unknown fields.
Timeouts are integers from 1 through 4294967, measured in seconds.
Configured command strings must not be empty and are executed through
.BR "sh -c" .
.PP
The optional
.B [general]
table accepts the following fields:
.TP
.B lock_command
Command run for a logind session lock request.
.TP
.B unlock_command
Command run for a logind session unlock request.
Leave this unset unless the locker provides a safe external unlock operation.
.TP
.B before_sleep_command
Command run before the system enters sleep.
.TP
.B after_resume_command
Command run after logind reports that the sleep operation finished or failed.
.TP
.B wait_before_sleep
When true, hold a logind delay inhibitor until the before-sleep command exits
or logind reports that the sleep operation completed or failed.
Logind may proceed after its maximum delay even if the inhibitor is still held.
Finishing the sleep cycle releases its inhibitor without stopping the command.
A still-running command can delay each later sleep attempt up to the maximum;
prefer a locker that daemonizes only after the session is locked.
Defaults to true.
.TP
.B ignore_dbus_inhibit
When true, do not provide or respect the
.B org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver
inhibition service.
Defaults to false.
.TP
.B ignore_systemd_inhibit
When true, do not use systemd-logind idle inhibitors to suppress listener
actions.
Defaults to false.
.PP
The optional
.B [idle_hint]
table has one required
.B timeout
field.
After that period of inactivity, sweetsidle reports the session as idle to
logind.
Activity, inhibition, unlock, resume, pause, and clean shutdown clear the hint.
.PP
Each
.B [[listener]]
table accepts:
.TP
.B timeout
Required inactivity period in seconds.
.TP
.B on_timeout
Optional command run when the timeout expires.
.TP
.B on_resume
Optional command run when activity returns after this listener timed out.
.TP
.B ignore_inhibit
When true, allow this listener to run despite compositor, ScreenSaver D-Bus,
and systemd inhibitors.
Defaults to false.
This policy requires version 2 of
.BR ext_idle_notifier_v1 .
.SH EXAMPLE CONFIGURATION
.EX
[general]
lock_command = "sweetslock"
before_sleep_command = "sweetslock --daemonize"
wait_before_sleep = true

[idle_hint]
timeout = 300

[[listener]]
timeout = 300
on_timeout = "sweetslock"
ignore_inhibit = true

[[listener]]
timeout = 600
on_timeout = "sweetsmsg output '*' power off"
on_resume = "sweetsmsg output '*' power on"
.EE
.SH INHIBITORS
Ordinary listeners respect compositor idle inhibitors, ScreenSaver D-Bus
inhibitors, and block-mode systemd-logind inhibitors whose operation list
contains
.BR idle .
The ScreenSaver interface is available at both
.I /org/freedesktop/ScreenSaver
and
.IR /ScreenSaver .
A listener with
.B ignore_inhibit = true
bypasses all three sources.
ScreenSaver inhibitors are released when their D-Bus client disconnects,
including during an Inhibit call.
.PP
The
.B status
command can list ScreenSaver and systemd inhibitor details.
The idle-notify protocol does not expose compositor inhibitor identities, so
they cannot be included in status output.
.SH CONTROL SOCKET
A running daemon owns
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sweetsidle.sock
with mode 0600.
The
.BR status ,
.BR pause ,
and
.B resume
commands use this local socket.
An abandoned socket is replaced on startup, while a live socket prevents a
second daemon instance from starting.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Stop the daemon cleanly.
Configured commands that are already running are left running.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Queue the same reload as the
.B reload
command without stopping the daemon.
Configuration and compositor compatibility validation failures are rejected
and the complete last valid configuration remains active.
Changes that would alter required D-Bus or logind integrations require a daemon
restart and are not applied partially.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to construct the default configuration path.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory containing the owner-only control socket.
Required by control commands and normal daemon startup.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Identifies the Wayland display used by the daemon.
.TP
.B XDG_SESSION_ID
Used when resolving the current logind session.
If unavailable, sweetsidle asks logind for the session associated with its
process ID.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sweetsidle/config.toml
Default user configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sweetsidle.sock
Local control socket.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/sweetsidle.service
Typical packaged location of the systemd user service.
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1/sweetsidle.1
Typical packaged location of this manual page.
.SH SYSTEMD USER SERVICE
The supplied
.B sweetsidle.service
unit runs the daemon as part of
.BR graphical-session.target .
After installing the binary, unit, and manual page, enable it with:
.PP
.EX
systemctl --user enable --now sweetsidle.service
.EE
.PP
Do not also launch sweetsidle from compositor configuration while the service
is enabled.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B sweetsidle
returns 0 after successful informational commands, validation, or clean daemon
shutdown.
It returns 2 for invalid arguments, configuration errors, control-socket
failures, and daemon startup or runtime failures.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate an explicit configuration:
.PP
.EX
sweetsidle --config ./config.toml --check-config
.EE
.PP
Run with verbose diagnostics:
.PP
.EX
sweetsidle --verbose --config ./config.toml
.EE
.PP
Read the paused state from JSON status output:
.PP
.EX
sweetsidle status --json | jq -r .paused
.EE
.PP
Reload the active configuration:
.PP
.EX
pkill -HUP -x sweetsidle
.EE
